# Copy to .env.local and set your own value. .env.local is git-ignored.

# One password for the authoring studio: it opens the studio and authorises
# everything inside it. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so it stays on the machine and
# is never sent to the browser — the server does the checking.
#
# The studio itself only exists while the app runs locally: its page and its
# routes are named *.dev.tsx / *.dev.ts, which `pageExtensions` drops from the
# static export. The published site has no studio and no password to find.
STUDIO_PASSWORD=change-me
